<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Irfan Habib</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1931</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Irfan Habib (born 1931) is an Indian historian of medieval and early modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, long associated with Aligarh Muslim University. His book The Agrarian System of Mughal India (1963) and his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlas-mountains">Atlas</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> made him one of the leading authorities on Mughal economy and society. Writing from a Marxist perspective, he has also published on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a>'s state and its attempts at modernisation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/irfan-habib.jpg" alt="Irfan Habib" width="320" height="265" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Amber Habib · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Irfan_Habib.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
